osition to be  able to call his shot right now  especially he's not that type of a  player first of all to where he's going  to kind of create a media frenzy around  him and people are going to be oh my  gosh duke johnson wants out of the  cleveland browns no he's a good player  but not a star or anything like that but  the ultimate point is this mike that you  know i think he's crazy for wanting to  be traded right now nick chubb's the  only guy he's got to worry about yes  kareem hunt's going to be there during  otas and training camp man that's going  to make practice better for you duke  johnson but the first eight weeks of the  year kareem hunt won't be there they  don't have that third down pass catching  back on their offensive roster right now  he is that guy so he really can be set  up to have a hell of a year the first  eight weeks of the year and we'll see  where kareem hun is at that point maybe  he's trade bait at that point i don't  know but i think he is a little early  here in calling his shot for the trade  because i i do believe that he's going  to have a nice little role within this  football team and in this offense  because they don't have anybody else at  the running back position that that  fills the need that he does is that  third down versatile pass catching back  yeah and look he's already gotten his  second contract from the cleveland  browns so this isn't about setting  himself up to get paid right  i just think that he feels marginalized  by the arrival of kareem hunt and the  the uh the rise of nick chubb and i  think that he sees the handwritings on  the wall at some point they're going to  decide we don't need duke johnson he's  trying to push that before it gets to  that point so he can land somewhere else  where he can make the team and justify  his salary i'm looking at what he's due  to make over the next few years 1.8  million this year that's not all that  much but he's going to have to get  himself in a spot where he justifies a  3.6 million dollar salary in 2020 and  4.65 million in 2021. that's a lot for  running backs when there are a lot of  guys out there you can draft and pay six  figures to i think this is why he's  trying to push this he wants to have a  chance to earn his money in 2020 and  2021 the browns aren't going to keep him  for that and he's going to have to go  out and scrounge around for the best  offer he can find whereas if he goes to  a team where he can make an impact this  year maybe they happily pay him 3.6  million next year especially if they  gave something up to get him now yeah  those are those are all valid points i  mean  you mean you're right i'm not going to  argue against any of those only thing  i'd argue against is that duke johnson  you're you're a part of a hell of an  offense right now that's got a lot of  talent and you can kind of be the under  the radar nobody's thinking about you  guy on that offense that can maybe  benefit from having so much talent  around you and like i said previously  the fact that there is no guy on the  roster that does the things duke johnson  does coming out of the backfield  especially in the past game where he  might be able to rack up enough stats  and carve out enough of a  niche for himself in that offense in the  first eight weeks of the year to where a  kareem hunt comes back we don't expect  him to be like totally a 100 kareem hunt  right right away in week nine so duke  johnson's still gonna have that role and  if things are going really well they're  not going to just be like oh kareem  hunts back the hell with you duke  johnson get off the field no he's going  to continue that role and set himself up  really for probably a trade in the  offseason however it goes with kareem  hunt or maybe he does get released and  has the stats that can justify the kind  of money you're talking about for that  2020 season to where he signs somewhere  else as a free agent and cleveland does  ultimately uh cut him so i'm just 